  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"24.12.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pulsectl\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/pulsectl/pulsectl-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 288d6715232ac6f3dcdb123fbecaa2c0b9a50ea4087e6e87c3f841ab0a8a07fc\n\nbuild:\n  number: 2\n  # ctypes bindings for PulseAudio (libpulse); the module dlopens libpulse.so\n  # at import time, and conda-forge only packages it (pulseaudio-client) for\n  # Linux, so this package is Linux-only.\n  skip: not linux\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python\n    - setuptools\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python\n    # pulsectl dlopens libpulse.so.0 via ctypes at import time\n    - pulseaudio-client\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - pulsectl\n      pip_check: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: Python high-level interface and ctypes-based bindings for PulseAudio (libpulse)\n  description: |\n    pulsectl provides a high-level Python interface on top of ctypes-based\n    bindings for libpulse. It can list and control sinks, sources, cards,\n    and per-application streams, adjust and track volumes, move streams\n    between devices, and subscribe to server-side events of a PulseAudio\n    or PipeWire (via pipewire-pulse) sound server.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: COPYING\n  homepage: https://pypi.org/project/pulsectl/\n  repository: https://github.com/mk-fg/python-pulse-control\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - ruben-arts\n",
